ing monthly debt, and an existing-customer flag \u2014 and returns one outcome (APPROVED, DECLINED or MANUAL_REVIEW) with, where an outcome is priced, a final APR. It holds no state and owns no workflow: it is a decision function behind one HTTP endpoint.","sourceFile":".kiro/specs/loan-decisioning/requirements.md","anchor":"requirements-document","line":1,"tags":[],"status":"NOTCOVERED","callCount":0,"tests":[]},{"id":"req:loan-decisioning.1","source":"req","name":"Input Validation","parent":"loan-decisioning","kind":"req","posture":"shared","decomposes":["loan-decisioning.1/1","loan-decisioning.1/2"],"acceptance":["WHEN the Decision_Service receives an Application with a missing required field, THEN THE Decision_Service SHALL reject the request and name the missing field.","WHEN the Decision_Service receives an Application whose Credit_Score is outside the range 300\u2013850, THEN THE Decision_Service SHALL reject the request and name the offending field."],"body":"**User Story:** As a caller of the Decision_Service, I want malformed Applications rejected before any decision is made, so that an Outcome is never derived from data the service could not understand.","sourceFile":".kiro/specs/loan-decisioning/requirements.md","anchor":"requirement-1-input-validation","line":28,"tags":[],"status":"COVERED","assertedProportion":1.0,"callCount":0,"tests":["decision-api.feature:a missing required field is rejected, naming the field","decision-api.feature:a credit score outside 300-850 is rejected, naming the field"]},{"id":"req:loan-decisioning.1/1","source":"req","name":"WHEN the Decision_Service receives an Application with a missing required field, THEN THE Decision_Service SHALL reject the request and name the missing field.","kind":"acceptance-criterion","parentReq":"loan-decisioning.1","criterion":"1","claimed":true,"claimedBy":"1","claimedTask":"Set up the decisioning module and its HTTP surface","tags":[],"status":"COVERED","assertedProportion":1.0,"callCount":0,"